  "description": "THE WIDTHS, and the FILLER spans that make them (gates G19, G20, G21). Every record on both channels is pinned as a complete image and every dataset carries its declared width, so this case fails immediately if any span is dropped: the generated transaction is 350 bytes, which is CVTRA05Y and also app/jcl/INTCALC.jcl:39's DCB=(RECFM=F,LRECL=350), and it is only 350 because TRAN-AMT occupies eleven bytes and the trailing FILLER X(20) is EMITTED AS SPACES rather than omitted; the account image is 300, which is only 300 because FILLER X(178) is emitted; the category balance is 50 with FILLER X(22), the disclosure group 50 with FILLER X(28), and the cross-reference 50 - which its fixture does NOT supply, measuring 36 bytes with the trailing FILLER X(14) absent, so the fourteen spaces are supplied once at seed time by the declared normalisation. Drop any one of those spans and the total width is wrong, which is why the width is the assertion rather than a comment about it. 500.00 at fifteen percent is 6.25 exactly.",
